# Fit List + details

Reference pages:

- `/customer-orders`: `src/app/(app)/customer-orders/CustomerOrdersTable.tsx` (Fit List + `OrderDetailsPanel`) inside `CustomerOrdersWorkspace.tsx`.
- `/customers`: `src/app/(app)/customers/CustomersTable.tsx` (Fit List + `CustomerDetailsPanel`) inside `CustomersWorkspace.tsx`.

When the user says **fit-list+details**, reuse this instead of a new two-pane layout, an inline-expanding row, or a popup for the selected row. The list half is the **Fit List** (full rules below). The right half is a details container for the selected row.

## Layout

- Inside `FitPage`, under the page title. The title row carries **Filter** (and any sort control) on the right; the filter itself is a left docked panel (**docked-filter-panel**).
- An optional **Add new …** button sits above the pair and opens a card.
- One row, `flex min-h-0 flex-1 gap-3`: the Fit List on the left, the details container on the right, each **50% wide** (`w-1/2 min-w-0`), both with the Fit List box chrome (`rounded-lg border border-stone-300 bg-white p-3`).
- Right-side docked panels opened from the details (products, addresses, and so on) keep **docked-panel-colors**.

## Selection drives the details

- One selected row feeds the details container. A `SelectionBridge` reads `useList().selectedId` and reports it to the parent.
- Changing the selection closes any open edit card.
- Nothing selected: the container reads **Select a …** centered (for example **Select an order.**).
- A new row follows the Fit List add-batch rule below, so the details show it.

## List rows

- No buttons on a row. The row's main identifier may stay a link. Rows do not edit.
- Row columns are the short identifying fields only. Everything else is in the details.

## Details header

- A fixed-height header with a bottom border. The name and number on the left (name in medium text, number in muted text), truncated if long.
- On the right, on one line, aligned with each other: icon controls (**Open**, **Print**, and any status controls) with no box around them, then a thin divider, then **Edit** and **Delete** in the Fit List chip (`RowButtons`, `editing={false}`).
- **Edit** opens the same card as **Add new**, filled with this row. **Save** and **Cancel** appear on that card only after a field changes.
- **Delete** asks for confirmation. **Working…** floats to its left, another click is ignored until the write finishes, and an error shows as a `DismissNote` under the header.
- **Open** (folder icon) opens a docked panel on the right. **Print** opens the print page in a new tab.

## Details body

- Scrolls inside the container, `space-y-2`.
- Each group is a bordered stone-50 box (`overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-stone-300 bg-stone-50`). A titled group has a highlighted block header across its top: stone-200 bar, bottom border, semibold `text-xs`. An untitled first group has no bar.
- Compact text: labels 11px muted, values 13px. Facts sit in 2 to 4 columns (`grid-cols-2`, `-3`, `-4`) with small gaps; long values wrap.
- Address pairs (**Ship to**, **Bill to**) sit side by side, each a group. **Notes** is a group, last, and it grows to fill the free height above a pinned summary (`Section fill`), with a small minimum so a short panel scrolls instead.
- A summary group (for example **Order summary**) can be pinned under the scrolling body (`shrink-0`) so it stays visible. Compute it from data the page already loaded, with one shared function, not a new query.
- Fields shown in the list stay out of the details unless the details need them.

## Fit List (full rules, kept whole)

Shared UI in `src/components/list/ListTable.tsx` (`ListTable`, `SelectableRow`, `RowButtons`, `useList`, `useListRow`). Styles in `src/app/globals.css` (`.list-table`).

### Format

- One selected row at a time (click row to select; zebra + teal selected).
- After rows are **inserted**: if **one** new row, select it; if **several**, select the **last one added**. Pagination reveals that row. First load of the list does not treat existing rows as added. If the parent knows insert order, pass `resumeId` of that last row so selection follows the add batch, not list sort.
- Each data row is a **full border box** (not a shared underline). First cell indented.
- Action buttons live in a **rounded bordered chip** in the **last column**. In fit-list+details the row has no chip. Edit and Delete move to the details header chip.
- Merchandise **Edit** opens the product settings popup (row does not expand). Charges still edit inline.

### Editing

- Only **one row** in edit mode.
- In edit: **Cancel** always; **Save** only if dirty; **Edit** when not editing. **Delete** optional.
- **Save** and **Delete** follow **Working…**: the label stays, Working… floats to the left, and another click is ignored until the write finishes.
- Click another row while **clean** → leave edit and select (or start edit if they clicked Edit).
- Click away while **dirty** → modal **Save** or **Cancel** (discard), then navigate.
- `tryLeave(fn)` for pagination or other navigation with the same prompt.

### Variants

- **Paged Fit List**: show as many full rows as fit; **Previous** / **Next**; optional outer **rounded bordered container**.
- Catalog pages with an **Add** row (`FitPage`): the list stretches in the leftover space so the add fields stay on screen (no page scroll to find Add). Inventory has no add row and fills the viewport.

Reuse this instead of inventing a new table/edit interaction.
